# M113 armored personnel carrier: the first TRACKED vehicle here, and the
# first model built around the 'track' block. A free-flying hull carries two
# independent track assemblies; each is a drive sprocket, a translational
# idler on a sliding tensioned carrier, five torsion-bar road-wheel stations,
# and a closed band of 63 shoes riding the lot. Hardpoints, masses, and
# inertias are the M113 data shipped with Project Chrono
# (data/vehicle/M113/), single-pin track variant:
#   vehicle/M113_Vehicle_SinglePin.json     track assemblies at y = +-1.0795
#   chassis/M113_Chassis.json               7819.24 kg hull
#   track_assembly/M113_TrackAssemblySinglePin_Left.json
#                                           sprocket/idler/suspension stations,
#                                           63 shoes
#   sprocket/M113_SprocketSinglePin_Left.json        10 teeth, assy radius 0.245
#   idler/M113_DoubleIdler_Left.json                 carrier + tensioner
#   idler_wheel/M113_DoubleIdlerWheel_Left.json      radius 0.255
#   suspension/M113_TranslationalDamperSuspension_Left.json   arm + torsion bar
#   road_wheel/M113_DoubleRoadWheel_Left.json        radius 0.305
#   track_shoe/M113_TrackShoeSinglePin.json          18.02 kg, pitch 0.154
#
# Axes are ISO vehicle: x forward, y outboard-left, z up. The BASE FRAME is
# Chrono's chassis reference frame, which for the M113 sits on the SPROCKET
# AXLE (the sprocket subsystem's location in the track assembly is exactly
# [0,0,0]): x = 0 at the drive sprocket, z = 0 at its axle height, y = 0 on
# the vehicle centerline. So the vehicle runs toward +x with the sprocket
# FORWARD and the idler at x = -3.95, which is how the real M113 is driven.
# A Chrono track-assembly hardpoint maps to this frame by adding the
# assembly's lateral offset (0, +-1.0795, 0) and then the subsystem's own
# location; left-side JSON values are used as given and the right side is the
# mirror image (negate y), exactly how Chrono mirrors one side to build the
# other. Both sides' revolute joints keep the +y axis (rather than mirroring
# the axis too), so equal q means the same physical motion left and right.
#
# Topology (27 hand-written bodies + 2 x 63 generated shoes = 153, nv 168,
# nc 4, mobility 164):
#   0  hull      floating   the whole 7819.24 kg sprung mass, free-flying
#                           (RBDA sec 9.4) with quaternion attitude, so no
#                           gimbal lock in any pitch/roll attitude. Everything
#                           else hangs off it. Unlike the wheeled models there
#                           are no shaker posts: a tracked vehicle's only path
#                           to the ground is through the band, so the hull is
#                           held up by the track contact forces (fext on the
#                           shoes) rather than by tire rods.
#
#   Left assembly bodies 1..13, right 14..26 (identical, y negated):
#     sprocket   revolute y  the drive member: 10 teeth, assembly radius 0.245.
#                            This is the DRIVE INPUT -- torque it through its
#                            own tau slot (Chrono drives it through
#                            M113_SimpleTrackDriveline; there is no driveline
#                            body here, the sprocket joint IS the input).
#     carrier    prismatic x idler carrier, sliding fore/aft on the hull
#                            (Chrono's TranslationalIdler: pitch angle 0, so
#                            the slide axis is exactly the hull x axis). The
#                            tensioner TSDA below pushes it rearward; its
#                            travel is what takes up track slack.
#     idler      revolute y  idler wheel, radius 0.255, on the carrier.
#     arm 1..5   revolute y  torsion-bar trailing arm, pivoting on the hull.
#                            The road wheel trails rearward and below the
#                            pivot (pivot->wheel = (-0.288, 0, -0.134), a
#                            0.318 m arm), so +q is jounce: it swings the
#                            wheel up and back. Carries the torsion bar as an
#                            rsda on this joint (see below).
#     wheel 1..5 revolute y  road wheel, radius 0.305, on its arm. Frame at
#                            the wheel center, which is where the arm's own
#                            revolute axis line passes -- Chrono puts the
#                            arm/wheel pin 0.12 inboard of the wheel center,
#                            but a revolute is indifferent to where along its
#                            axis the frame sits, so this is exact.
#
# Track bands (one 'track' block per side, each expanding into 63 shoe bodies
# -- a floating anchor shoe plus 62 revolute-y pins -- and ONE point-on-line
# closure loop, the planar-loop rule): the band lies in the assembly's x-z
# plane at y = +-1.0795 and rides the seven rollers listed in the block. The
# shoe chain is parented to the BASE, not the hull, exactly like the
# quartercar spindle: it is held in place by contact, not by a mount.
#
#   ONE FIDELITY NOTE. The loader's belt is the taut band around the TWO 'end'
#   pulleys only (sprocket + idler), so at the design pose its lower run is
#   the straight sprocket-to-idler tangent and the five road wheels, whose
#   bottoms reach z = -0.52, poke through it. The real lower run is pushed
#   down onto the road wheels. Consequences: the design-pose shoe positions
#   along the bottom are high by up to ~0.15 m, and the band perimeter comes
#   out 9.4745 m rather than 63 x 0.154 = 9.702 m, so the generated link
#   length is 0.15039 rather than the real 0.154 pitch (2.3% short -- almost
#   exactly the road-wheel wrap the two-pulley idealization leaves out). The
#   band is dynamically correct either way (63 shoes, correct mass/inertia,
#   a closed chain); it is the initial geometry that is idealized.
#
# Force elements (18: 10 torsion bars, 6 shocks, 2 tensioners; 16 POIs):
#   torsion_[LR][1-5]  rsda on the arm joint. Chrono's torsional spring is
#                      k = 2.5e4 Nm/rad, c = 5e2, free angle 0, preload
#                      -1e4 Nm. This format's rsda has no separate preload
#                      term, but a constant torque IS a shifted rest angle:
#                      tau = -k(q - q0) has tau(0) = k*q0, so q0 = preload/k
#                      = -0.4 rad reproduces it exactly. The sign checks out
#                      physically -- negative tau at q = 0 pushes the wheel
#                      down and back, which is the torsion bar holding the
#                      hull up.
#   shock_[LR][1,2,5]  tsda, the translational damper. Only stations 1, 2 and
#                      5 have one ("Has Shock" in the assembly JSON); k = 0,
#                      c = 1e2 N/(m/s), design length 0.6317 (used as l0, which
#                      a pure damper never reads). Both anchors ride the body
#                      that physically carries them -- hull above, arm below --
#                      so with the hull free the element measures only arm
#                      rotation, never a spurious length change from hull
#                      heave (the halfcar lesson).
#   tens_[LR]          tsda, the idler tensioner: k = 1e6 N/m, c = 1.4e4,
#                      free length 0.75, preload 2e4 N. Preload folds into the
#                      free length the same way (f = k(l - l0) is tension
#                      here, so l0 = 0.75 + 2e4/1e6 = 0.77). At the design
#                      pose the anchors are 0.5 apart, well inside l0, so the
#                      element pushes -- driving the carrier rearward, which
#                      is exactly how it tensions the track.
#   All passive (no 'input'). Chrono's nonlinear shock/tensioner maps are not
#   used; these are the linear JSON coefficients.
#
# WHAT HOLDS THIS UP. Two contact engines in series, both external to the
# generated dynamics and both applied through 'fext' (shoes, sprockets, idlers
# and road wheels all carry 'fext 1'), exactly as the wheeled models take tire
# loads through their spindles:
#
#   src/contact/track_contact.h   shoe pins against the seven rollers per side
#   src/contact/ground_contact.h  shoe pads against the terrain, via the
#                                 'ground' block at the foot of this file
#
# So the load path is ground -> pad -> shoe -> pin -> road wheel -> trailing arm
# -> torsion bar -> hull, which is the real one. Neither engine touches the
# generated code; both are caller-side force producers.
#
# At the DESIGN POSE this is still not an equilibrium, and deliberately so: the
# belt wraps only the two end pulleys, so the road wheels poke 0.17-0.25 m
# through the lower run and each tensioner sits 0.27 m inside its free length
# with no track tension yet to react it, shoving its carrier rearward at
# ~2.7e5 N. src/sim/main.c ramps both engines' stiffness in over 0.2 s and lets
# the band relax through the same force law that runs afterwards, rather than
# through a separate assembly path.
#
# q layout (nq 171, nv 168): hull q[0..6] (quat + pos) v[0..5]; then the 26
# assembly joints one slot each; then each band's anchor shoe (quat + pos 7 /
# spatial 6) followed by its 62 pins. Design pose is q = 0 with quaternions at
# identity for the hand-written bodies; the SHOES are the exception -- a
# closed band cannot sit at q = 0, so the loader writes their curved design
# pose into m->q0 and consumers seed q from there.

gravity 0 0 -9.81
stab 0.05

body                     # 0: hull, full M113 sprung mass, free-flying
parent -1
joint floating
tree 0 0 0
mass 7819.24
cg -2.006 0 0.406
inertia 13983.08 27287.61 28805.57 0 0 0
fext 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Left track assembly (y = +1.0795)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

body                     # 1: sprocket L (drive input)
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree 0 1.0795 0
mass 27.68
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.646 0.883 0.646 0 0 0
fext 1                   # contact reaction from the track band

body                     # 2: idler carrier L, slides fore/aft on the hull
parent 0
joint prismatic x
tree -3.95 1.0795 -0.12  # frame at the idler axle (a prismatic joint does not
mass 10.0                # care where along its axis the frame sits)
cg 0 -0.1 0
inertia 0.04 0.04 0.04 0 0 0

body                     # 3: idler wheel L, radius 0.255
parent 2
joint revolute y
tree 0 0 0
mass 25.76
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.618 1.12 0.618 0 0 0
fext 1                   # contact reaction from the track band

body                     # 4: arm L1 (torsion-bar trailing arm)
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -0.367 0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 5: road wheel L1, radius 0.305
parent 4
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 6: arm L2
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -1.034 0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 7: road wheel L2
parent 6
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 8: arm L3
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -1.701 0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 9: road wheel L3
parent 8
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 10: arm L4
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -2.368 0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 11: road wheel L4
parent 10
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 12: arm L5
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -3.034 0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 13: road wheel L5
parent 12
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Right track assembly (y = -1.0795), the mirror image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

body                     # 14: sprocket R (drive input)
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree 0 -1.0795 0
mass 27.68
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.646 0.883 0.646 0 0 0
fext 1                   # contact reaction from the track band

body                     # 15: idler carrier R
parent 0
joint prismatic x
tree -3.95 -1.0795 -0.12
mass 10.0
cg 0 0.1 0
inertia 0.04 0.04 0.04 0 0 0

body                     # 16: idler wheel R
parent 15
joint revolute y
tree 0 0 0
mass 25.76
cg 0 0 0
inertia 0.618 1.12 0.618 0 0 0
fext 1                   # contact reaction from the track band

body                     # 17: arm R1
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -0.367 -0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 18: road wheel R1
parent 17
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 -0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 19: arm R2
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -1.034 -0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 20: road wheel R2
parent 19
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 -0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 21: arm R3
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -1.701 -0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 22: road wheel R3
parent 21
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 -0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 23: arm R4
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -2.368 -0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 24: road wheel R4
parent 23
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 -0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

body                     # 25: arm R5
parent 0
joint revolute y
tree -3.034 -0.9595 -0.081
mass 75.26
cg -0.144 0 -0.067
inertia 0.37 0.77 0.77 0 0 0

body                     # 26: road wheel R5
parent 25
joint revolute y
tree -0.288 -0.12 -0.134
mass 35.56
cg 0 0 0
inertia 1.14 2.16 1.14 0 0 0
fext 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Torsion bars: one per road-wheel station, on the arm's own joint.
# q0 = preload/k = -1e4 / 2.5e4 = -0.4 rad reproduces Chrono's preload.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rsda torsion_L1
joint 4
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_L2
joint 6
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_L3
joint 8
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_L4
joint 10
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_L5
joint 12
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_R1
joint 17
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_R2
joint 19
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_R3
joint 21
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_R4
joint 23
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

rsda torsion_R5
joint 25
k 2.5e4
c 5e2
q0 -0.4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shocks: stations 1, 2 and 5 only. Hull anchor above, arm anchor below;
# design length 0.6317 (a pure damper never reads l0).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

poi shock_L1_hull  0 -0.955 0.9595 0.085
poi shock_L1_arm   4 -0.104 0 -0.240
tsda shock_L1
from shock_L1_hull
to shock_L1_arm
k 0
c 1e2
l0 0.63174

poi shock_L2_hull  0 -1.622 0.9595 0.085
poi shock_L2_arm   6 -0.104 0 -0.240
tsda shock_L2
from shock_L2_hull
to shock_L2_arm
k 0
c 1e2
l0 0.63174

poi shock_L5_hull  0 -3.622 0.9595 0.085
poi shock_L5_arm  12 -0.104 0 -0.240
tsda shock_L5
from shock_L5_hull
to shock_L5_arm
k 0
c 1e2
l0 0.63174

poi shock_R1_hull  0 -0.955 -0.9595 0.085
poi shock_R1_arm  17 -0.104 0 -0.240
tsda shock_R1
from shock_R1_hull
to shock_R1_arm
k 0
c 1e2
l0 0.63174

poi shock_R2_hull  0 -1.622 -0.9595 0.085
poi shock_R2_arm  19 -0.104 0 -0.240
tsda shock_R2
from shock_R2_hull
to shock_R2_arm
k 0
c 1e2
l0 0.63174

poi shock_R5_hull  0 -3.622 -0.9595 0.085
poi shock_R5_arm  25 -0.104 0 -0.240
tsda shock_R5
from shock_R5_hull
to shock_R5_arm
k 0
c 1e2
l0 0.63174

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Idler tensioners: hull anchor forward of the carrier anchor, so the
# compressed spring drives the carrier rearward and tensions the band.
# l0 = free length + preload/k = 0.75 + 2e4/1e6 = 0.77.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

poi tens_L_hull     0 -3.45 0.8795 -0.12
poi tens_L_carrier  2 0 -0.2 0
tsda tens_L
from tens_L_hull
to tens_L_carrier
k 1e6
c 1.4e4
l0 0.77

poi tens_R_hull     0 -3.45 -0.8795 -0.12
poi tens_R_carrier 15 0 0.2 0
tsda tens_R
from tens_R_hull
to tens_R_carrier
k 1e6
c 1.4e4
l0 0.77

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two track bands. 63 single-pin shoes each, riding sprocket + idler (the
# two path-defining 'end' pulleys) and the five road wheels. Ground plane at
# z = -0.55: the design-pose band centerline on the bottom run sits at the
# road-wheel bottom, z = -0.215 - 0.305 = -0.52, and the shoe pad reaches
# 0.03 below its own frame.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

track band_L
root 0
plane xz
shoes 63
pitch 0.154
mass 18.02
cg 0.0752 0 0          # link midpoint: half the generated link length
inertia 0.22 0.04 0.25 0 0 0
fext 1
roller 1 0.245 end drive teeth 10   # sprocket (assembly radius, not addendum)
roller 3 0.255 end                  # idler wheel
roller 5 0.305                      # road wheel 1
roller 7 0.305                      # road wheel 2
roller 9 0.305                      # road wheel 3
roller 11 0.305                     # road wheel 4
roller 13 0.305                     # road wheel 5
pad -0.03 0.12 0.36                 # ground pad: face 0.03 below the pin line,
                                    # inset from the 0.1504 link so adjacent
                                    # pads do not stack corners on shared pins
kn 2e5
kt 2e5
mu 0.8

track band_R
root 0
plane xz
shoes 63
pitch 0.154
mass 18.02
cg 0.0752 0 0
inertia 0.22 0.04 0.25 0 0 0
fext 1
roller 14 0.245 end drive teeth 10
roller 16 0.255 end
roller 18 0.305
roller 20 0.305
roller 22 0.305
roller 24 0.305
roller 26 0.305
pad -0.03 0.12 0.36
kn 2e5
kt 2e5
mu 0.8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GROUND. Flat, at z = -0.55: the settled lower run rests on the road wheels
# (centres z = -0.215, radius 0.305, so the pin line lands at -0.52) and the pad
# face is 0.03 below that. The design pose above is therefore ALREADY the ride
# height -- the vehicle needs no drop, which is why src/sim/main.c only ever
# lifts a model clear of the ground and never lowers one onto it.
#
# kn is sized per contact point: 208 pads carry the 1.11e5 N vehicle weight at
# about 534 N each, so 1.1e5 N/m gives ~5 mm sinkage. That is deliberately close
# to the band's own kn 2e5, so the two springs in series contribute comparable
# deflection and neither one dominates the ride height.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ground
plane 0 0 1 -0.55
kn 1.1e5
mu 0.8
